{
  "id": "great-commission-03",
  "checkpoint": 3,
  "title": "Grace, Faith and Redemption",
  "summary": "Paul explica a mensagem central do Evangelho: como a graça imerecida de Deus, a redenção em Cristo e uma aliança de fé trazem reconciliação e salvação.",
  "audio_url": "/audios/great-commission-03.mp3",
  "word_count_target": 140,
  "story_en": "The young man leans forward, eager to understand how forgiveness works. Paul opens a small pocket Bible to explain the message of hope clearly.\n\n“Salvation is not earned by our own good deeds,” Paul explains gently. “It is a free gift received purely by grace through genuine faith.”\n\nHe describes how human brokenness separated us from God, creating a need for true reconciliation. Through Christ’s sacrifice on the cross, full redemption was paid for our past, present, and future.\n\n“God offers an everlasting covenant built on his deep mercy,” Paul continues. “When we trust Him, our debt is completely cleared, and our relationship with the Father is restored.”\n\nTears well up in the listener's eyes as the weight of guilt lifts from his heart. For the first time, he understands the beauty of God’s redeeming love.",
